-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
What is not here
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the public source repository. It is published from a private one by an
allowlist, so it holds the product and nothing else: no strategy documents, no
field measurements, no infrastructure or credentials, no internal notes. Files
absent from this repository are absent on purpose and are not missing.

The published history is a sequence of synthesised commits rather than a mirror
of the private one. A secret that had ever touched the private history would
become permanent public history the moment the two were joined, and a public
repository cannot be recalled once it has been cloned.
